{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef read_data():\n    return list(map(int, sys.stdin.read().split()))\n\ndef main():\n    data = read_data()\n    n, mod = data[0], data[1]\n    \n    if n == 0:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[1] = 1\n    \n    for val in range(2, n + 1):\n        ans = 1  # contribution from mem[1]\n        limit = int(val ** 0.5) + 1\n        \n        # Sum over divisor parts\n        for d in range(2, limit):\n            ans = (ans + dp[val // d]) % mod\n        \n        # Handle remaining intervals using division grouping\n        start = val\n        group = 1\n        while group <= val // limit:\n            end = val // (group + 1)\n            ans = (ans + (start - end) * dp[group]) % mod\n            start = end\n            group += 1\n        \n        dp[val] = ans\n    \n    print(dp[n] % mod)\n\nmain()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        \n        // Read all input data\n        List<Integer> dataList = new ArrayList<>();\n        while (scanner.hasNextInt()) {\n            dataList.add(scanner.nextInt());\n        }\n        \n        int[] data = new int[dataList.size()];\n        for (int i = 0; i < dataList.size(); i++) {\n            data[i] = dataList.get(i);\n        }\n        \n        int n = data[0];\n        int mod = data[1];\n        \n        if (n == 0) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        int[] dp = new int[n + 1];\n        dp[1] = 1;\n        \n        for (int val = 2; val <= n; val++) {\n            int ans = 1; // contribution from mem[1]\n            int limit = (int) Math.sqrt(val) + 1;\n            \n            // Sum over divisor parts\n            for (int d = 2; d < limit; d++) {\n                ans = (ans + dp[val / d]) % mod;\n            }\n            \n            // Handle remaining intervals using division grouping\n            int start = val;\n            int group = 1;\n            while (group <= val / limit) {\n                int end = val / (group + 1);\n                ans = (ans + (start - end) * dp[group]) % mod;\n                start = end;\n                group++;\n            }\n            \n            dp[val] = ans;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(dp[n] % mod);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.331102824537084e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.082063141046092e-05, -6.818538531661034e-05, -0.11282873898744583, -0.11532334983348846, -9.417489309271332e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.421248038648628e-05, -0.038043707609176636, -0.002477792324498296, -0.0009635811438784003, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.000674616196192801, -0.00014256415306590497, -5.364403477869928e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.0040289857424796e-05, -5.960462772236497e